### Module facts (from M1-M5 ## Modules)
- standards L9 849 lines: kinds statute, regulation, ordinance, court, policy, commitment; R1 declare, R2 text required, R3 profile standard_sources match, R5 passageNotice, R6 supersedes one successor, R7 inForce, R8 standardsIn at, R9-10 propose/adopt; TEXTS_MAX 50; no internal structure; UI 0 all ops; no AI caller (PLANE_OPS lacks standardpropose); used by conformance, filings, action-plans (9), 11 only.
- conformance L9 1539: determine rests on published findings (publication.publishedEditionsOf); actor {role, body}; R3 in force at act's date; UI 0.
- actions L9 2884: only layer-9 module member reaches (actionmove, actioncorrespond, actionlaws, actionrisktier); R48 pressure marks; R52-R60 litigation hold (UI 0 actionhold etc); R9 addressee office, person check via entities.readEntity; clock date-only UTC; N521 device half unbuilt.
- action-clocks L9 885: start events filed/received only (act, known undetermined); weekend hard-coded; no roll-forward; UTC; time_zone/hours never used; clockPropose no op.
- filings L9 2035: counselPacket :1142; chronology :1018-1046 covers only one action's act, findings' ratification dates, state history, correspondence, clock; day-truncated; theoryPropose :1417; availableActions :1548; UI 0 all 11 ops; AI no caller; instance sending "not in this version... Bob's to add (K102)" filings.txt:122.
- escalation L9 1833: 7 stages; stage 5 legal tools R8; R12 elected/oversight flags; UI 0.
- filing-templates L9 1719: brief templates; UI 0.
- jurisdictions L1 1533: R23 standard_sources kind court; R25 venue how court; R26 deadlines applies_to claim; R32 legal_organisations; R39 evidence; R40 templates. Oakland: 2026 holidays only 3 entries (Superior Court venue M-189 ...); 1 deadline records_response; no claim deadline; 13 action kinds incl records_petition (Tier 2, Alameda Superior Court), consent_decree_motion, taxpayer_action, assessment_challenge, constitutional_claim; legal_organisations HJTA, First Amendment Coalition; no layer 6-8 module uses jurisdictions.
- docprofile L1 3170: doctypes meeting-minutes, meeting-agenda, meeting-calendar, regulation, staff-report, staff-directory, generic; readers emit reference kinds instrument, code_section, legislation, meeting, contact; dates parsed only "Month D, YYYY" UTC; temporal connections not stored.
- extraction L4: reading's at = capture retrieved instant; no document date.
- content L4: extents, passageText; UI 0 direct.
- entities L5 1326: ENTITY_KINDS source, institution, office, movement, person, body, ordinance, parcel, contract, fund; RELATION_KINDS proxy_for, member_of, overlaps; UI reaches entitycreate, relationdeclare etc.
- connections L5: agenda->file containment built, UI 0.
- progressions L5 1669: declared flows, threaded instances, missing/overdue; intervals fixed ms; anchor = capture time not doc date; no tz/business days; UI reaches progression, progressiondefine, thread, discharge (member CAN reach!). AI none.
- inquiry L6: NORM_CANONS bare tokens; nothing ranks norms.
- run modes: check (deployed), investigate, extract, plan (not deployed). One model call site agent-worker/src/model.mjs; DEFAULT_MODEL claude-opus-5; installer sets no Claude key -> NO_ACCOUNT_RESOLVED; UI never calls airunopen; agent-worker binding INERT. Skill pack investigative-session only; action_planning layer lists theorypropose etc; PLANE_OPS writes only suggest, capturerequest, optionpropose, airuntick, airunclose.
- retrieval L5: registerActionFacts etc; query time fields string compare.
- reevaluation L7: R30/R33 publication docket moves (contested since filing instant); not court.
- monitoring L10 3363: watches docs at cadence (hourly..monthly; per_meeting null); R67 docket watch reads another group's published-case docket daily; deadlineRecheck UTC; legal_deadline_approaching typed reason no link; UI 0 all ops (member sees queue items); monitor op member session.
- acquisition L3: Memento always asks now (no as-of past retrieval); acquire UI 9.
- sources L3: disclosure history publishableAt({at}) template for position-holders over time; UI 0.
- affordances L11: correspondence_stages; ACTS only info/inquiry/action/project; layer-9 acts NON_ACTS never offered per object.
- queue L11: litigation-hold To-do (R1/R12); due YYYY-MM-DD UTC; UI never calls per-kind doors.
- publication L8: publishedEditionsOf.
- Member reach COURTS (M5): 18 ops; called 2 (actioncorrespond, actionrisktier). "No op in the 446 names a court case, docket of a court, party, filing in a court, order or judgment as an object."

### Primary-source findings
- standards R1 kinds statute..court..; R2 text required (captured); R3 profile match or undetermined; R6 supersedes one successor ("an amendment, a renumbering, a later decision"); R7 inForce; R9/R10 proposal/adopt (Legal/Policy Lookup skill); instance-wide not project's (Suggestions); no internal structure.
- progressions: instance = (progression key, entity id); thread placements of captures resolving to entity; R11 missing_predecessor; R14 discharge with exception doc + citation; R16 overdue within interval <n> day|week|month|year, from reading's date (= capture time) else registration; calendar only; R24 derived on read; R25 finding reports never decides; R32 junction deferred. Member UI reaches progressiondefine/thread/discharge. => a proceeding's procedural flow could be a declared progression keyed on a proceeding entity — but intervals are calendar, from capture instant, not filed date; court rules (business days/court holidays) absent.
- entities: kinds closed (no proceeding/case kind; person exists); relations 3 closed; R26 constitutive never traversed; R9 recogniser A/B/C by alias/ref_key/label; DEC-52 machine may declare (class:<cls>).
- jurisdictions R25 venue how court; R26 deadlines applies_to claim, starts received|filed|act|known; R33 holidays per year; R39 evidence; R32 legal orgs; R43 holidays offices incl venue kind (court's holiday entry offices [{venue: records_petition}] K934). No court/proceeding vocabulary (case number patterns!). R6 vocabulary has file_numbers for legislative record, codes — could add a `case_numbers` vocabulary key (profile data) for docket-number recognition.
- monitoring: any public https locator watched at cadence; R52 legal_deadline_approaching reason; R67 docket watch = other group's published-case docket (JSON), NOT court.
- capture-sources R55-R63 member-supplied per-host credentials (login, user-agent, other), encrypted, capture marked not reproducible by public; BUILT (credentials.mjs; capture-requests drain :782). Applies only to a refused capture retried via capture-requests (AI/daemon path).
- layers.md: layer 9 contract text; Layer 9 rationale "After publication, because a finding is published before a group acts on it"; standards row: "Which laws and bodies exist comes from the jurisdiction profile". Bob's ruling 5: adding module carrying product capability / changing layer -> Bob.
- modules.json order: ... progressions(38) bias observation-log query-language retrieval(42) | inquiry-grammar(43)... agent-worker(55) | intent, reevaluation (56-57) | case-grammar(58).. review(71) | local-facts(72) standards(73) conformance(74)... action-plans(82) | monitoring(83) link-sweep scheduler(85).
- Journeys §3 L106: "A court case or legal proceeding | Reading about a lawsuit the city is a party to | Capture the filings, name the parties and offices involved, and watch the court's docket page for new filings | Questions about what the filings show; the case's deadlines kept in view (journeys 7 and 14)". L111 regulatory proceeding: "A utility's rate case before a state commission | Capture the filings and follow the proceeding's docket | Questions on the record as it builds; filing deadlines in the plan (journeys 13 and 14)". L122 lawyers start from filings. §6 L531 Following a court case gap; L533 offices and who held them needed by court case row.
- Roadmap §1 L253-258 (CPRA 10-day expired, three enforcement threats); L267-274 legal pathways report & key precedents; L276-281 OPD consent decree 23-year, EPA consent decree, Prop 218 litigation; §2 L285-303 "The city CAN ignore court orders, grand jury findings, CPRA deadlines; what it cannot ignore is SUSTAINED ATTENTION applied through legal mechanisms"; App B L1081-1105 CPRA sections, filing fee $435, grand jury PC 925a etc, precedents, Livermore settlement, CCP 526a, anti-SLAPP CCP 425.16.
- Runtime: Workers Paid required (DEC-42); subrequests 10000 in wrangler (DIST §6); platforms terminate at wall/CPU (TAD §10.7); scheduler one alarm; monitoring tick budget 50.

### Web research findings (cite URLs)
- CourtListener API v4: token/basic auth; "Many of our APIs are open by default" but add auth before deploying; default authenticated 5/min, 50/hour, 125/day rolling; FLP membership expands; webhooks for docket updates, search alerts, RECAP Fetch completion. https://wiki.free.law/c/courtlistener/help/api/rest/v4/overview
- RECAP Fetch: free API but uses your PACER credentials to purchase; needs CL token + PACER user/password. https://wiki.free.law/c/courtlistener/help/api/rest/v4/recap
- Docket alerts: PACER (federal) cases; 5 free daily alerts; FLP member $10/mo (5 real-time, 10 daily) to $100/mo; webhooks. https://www.lawnext.com/2025/06/courtlistener-launches-recap-search-alerts-for-pacer-filings-google-alerts-for-federal-courts.html ; https://wiki.free.law/c/courtlistener/help/alerts/docket-alerts-for-pacer
- PACER: $0.10/page, cap $3/document (30 pages) for docs and case-specific reports incl docket report; no cap for name search, non-case reports, transcripts; ≤$30/quarter waived; 75% pay nothing. https://pacer.uscourts.gov/help/faqs/how-much-does-it-cost-access-documents-using-pacer
- RECAP archive: documents bought on PACER contributed back; public domain; free. https://free.law/ (and https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/RECAP)
- CourtListener removal policy: no removal of public doc without court order; redaction per court order with note; blocks search indexing on request. https://wiki.free.law/c/terms/courtlistener/courtlistenercom-content-removal-policy
- eyecite: extracts full, short form, supra, id., ibid. https://pypi.org/project/eyecite/2.0.0 ; Citation Lookup API: text ≤64,000 chars, 250 citations/request, 60 valid citations/min, auth required; built on eyecite; guardrail vs hallucinated citations. https://wiki.free.law/c/courtlistener/help/api/rest/v4/citation-lookup ; https://free.law/2024/04/16/citation-lookup-api/
- reporters-db JSON: 1,167 reporters, 2,102 variations; Walverine Node module. https://free.law/projects/reporters-db ; courts-db https://pypi.org/project/courts-db/0.10.24
- Juriscraper: opinions from all state courts of last resort, dozens of intermediate appellate, all federal appeals; >200 webpages daily. https://free.law/projects/juriscraper
- Caselaw Access Project: 6.4M published US cases 1658-2018?; commercial restrictions ended March 2024; static. https://www.lawnext.com/2024/03/event-tomorrow-marks-the-end-of-commercial-restrictions-on-the-caselaw-access-project-that-digitized-all-u-s-case-law.html
- OASIS ECF 5.0: NIEM 4.0 conformant; docket entry ("an entry in the docket or register of actions for a case"), court event actor, party roles; case types bankruptcy, civil, criminal, domestic relations, juvenile, traffic. https://docs.oasis-open.org/legalxml-courtfiling/ecf/v5.0/cs01/model/niem-mapping.html ; https://niem.gov/node/708
- California CRC 2.503: civil records remote electronic access "to the extent feasible"; criminal, family, juvenile, civil harassment etc courthouse-only. https://courts.ca.gov/cms/rules/index/two/rule2_503
- Alameda eCourt portal: by case number read parties, Register of Actions, minutes, future hearing dates; document download $1/page first 5 pages, $.50 thereafter, cap $50/doc (fetched page); civil/family/probate only, not criminal. https://eportal.alameda.courts.ca.gov/?q=node/388
- Grand jury responses PC 933.05: agree/disagree per finding; per recommendation implemented / will be (timeframe) / further analysis (≤6 months) / not implemented with explanation; 60 days elected officers, 90 days governing bodies (PC 933(c)). https://california.public.law/codes/penal_code_section_933.05 ; https://www.santacruzcountyca.gov/Portals/0/County/GrandJury/GJ2009_responses/Instructions.htm ; courts publish response compliance reports e.g. https://www.placer.courts.ca.gov/sites/default/files/Response%20Report%20for%202022-2023.pdf
- OPD NSA: 2003, 51 tasks; independent monitor quarterly reports; reports 2010-2025 on city site; released 2025? (KQED). https://www.oaklandca.gov/Public-Safety-Streets/Police/OPD-Policies-and-Resources/OPD-Independent-Monitor-Report-2010-2025 ; https://www.kqed.org/news/12101833/a-new-beginning-oakland-police-to-exit-federal-oversight-after-23-years
- Consent decree compliance levels Preliminary, Secondary, Full per paragraph (Chicago IMR; Newark DOJ). https://www.chicago.gov/content/dam/city/depts/cpb/supp_info/IMR8PBParagraphs.pdf ; https://www.justice.gov/crt/case-document/file/1365081/download ; Chicago 552 paragraphs, some compliance 433 (WTTW) https://news.wttw.com/2022/12/16/chicago-police-must-significantly-improve-community-partnership-efforts-independent
- CPUC: docket card per formal proceeding (applications/rate cases, rulemakings, investigations, complaints): filings by parties, rulings, decisions; service list Parties vs Information Only; subscription service; proceeding numbers like A.12-03-004. https://webproda.cpuc.ca.gov/about-cpuc/divisions/news-and-public-information-office/public-advisors-office/tracking-issues-of-interest ; https://www.cpuc.ca.gov/-/media/cpuc-website/files/legacyfiles/h/11314-how-to-become-a-party-in-a-cpuc-proceeding.pdf ; https://www.cpuc.ca.gov/proceedings-and-rulemaking
- Regulations.gov API v4: dockets/documents/comments; api.data.gov key, 1,000 req/hour; no bulk. https://open.gsa.gov/api/regulationsgov/
- Settlements tracking: FiveThirtyEight/Marshall Project datasets 31 cities 2010-2019 (date of incident, lawsuit filed, amount, outcome, allegations); Chicago $210M 2012-2015. https://www.kuow.org/stories/tracking-police-misconduct-settlements-that-cost-cities-millions
- Court watch: Court Watch NOLA 130 volunteers, 1,110 visits, 7,000 cases, observation forms; annual report. https://www.openphilanthropy.org/wp-content/uploads/Court_Watch_NOLA_CDC_Annual_Report_2016.pdf
- Audit rec follow-up: auditors track recommendations in database; semi-annual status (Implemented, In process, ...); Seattle 72% of 833 implemented. https://seattle.gov/documents/Departments/CityAuditor/auditreports/RecFollowUp2021_FINAL.pdf ; https://www.sandiego.gov/auditor/reports/recommendation-follow-dashboard
- CA AG opinions: advisory, not binding, "entitled to great weight"/"considerable weight". https://oag.ca.gov/node/6 ; https://hooperlundy.com/news-pdf/?pdf=929
- Journalists: docket alerts, RECAP; sealed docs not in PACER, motions to unseal. https://free.law/2018/08/21/announcing-pacer-docket-alerts-for-journalists-lawyers-researchers-and-the-public/ ; https://journalistsresource.org/?p=75500 ; https://foreignpress.org/journalism-resources/mining-court-dockets-is-a-valuable-journalistic-skill
- UPL: legal information vs advice (applying law to a person's facts). https://judicature.duke.edu/articles/legal-information-vs-legal-advice-a-25-year-retrospective/
- Cloudflare Workers Paid: 10,000 subrequests default, up to 10M configurable; CPU 30s default up to 5 min; waiting on fetch not CPU. https://developers.cloudflare.com/workers/platform/limits ; https://developers.cloudflare.com/changelog/2026-02-11-subrequests-limit

